    "created_at": "2024-09-23T17:44:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-23T17:44:53Z",
    "body": "Right, its set during [fetching](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch) and then never touched again:\r\n> If request’s [origin](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-origin) is \"client\", then set request’s [origin](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-origin) to request’s [client](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-client)’s [origin](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-settings-object-origin).\r\n\r\nAdding an assert seems reasonable. There are more places where its not immediately obvious that they are only called when the origin cannot be `\"client\"`, like [`append a request origin header`](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#append-a-request-origin-header). I assume those should get an assert too?\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
